Key message 2: Leveraging their individual strengths, Moroccan ports can contribute to the development of an integrated green hydrogen value chain across the country.
While none of the ports analyzed provides ideal conditions for covering the full range of value creation from green hydrogen generation to usage, they all have unique individual strengths.
A scenario analysis shows that by strategically integrating each port into a value chain leveraging their individual strengths, the overall costs at the national level can be minimized.

For each of these four ports, the technical and financial viability of green hydrogen-based shipping fuel production, supply, storage, bunkering, and export are assessed. Individual strengths and weaknesses of the ports are summarized in Table E.1.

