The hydrogen market is expected to be primarily regionally oriented rather than globally
(IRENA, 2022b). Even though shipping costs are a minor component in the LCOH, it is more economical to supply the demand centers from nearby production centers, provided that the volumes are sufficient to meet demand.

Latin America, Australia, the Middle East, and North Africa are likely to become the main exporting regions globally, while Europe, Japan, and the Republic of Korea will become the main importing regions (IRENA, 2022b). North Africa will export mainly to Europe, Australia will export mainly to
Asia, and the Americas will export to Asia and Europe.
