Bank, African Union, and International Solar Alliance (2022) have estimated that Morocco and
Mauritania combined could export up to 7.5 mtpa of hydrogen as soon as 2035. In this scenario,
4 out of 7 electrolyzers are located in Morocco, enabling a production of 4.28 mtpa. IRENA (2023a)
has estimated Morocco’s hydrogen export potential at 4.41 mtpa of hydrogen in 2040. Lastly, the European Hydrogen4EU (2022) initiative estimates a total export from Morocco of 5.3 mtpa in
