Tanger Med’s most likely primary role in the development of hydrogen and ammonia value chains lies in the import and application of these fuels in bunkering. It is also evident that the port is experiencing fast growth and has limitations in terms of space and interference with current activities and infrastructure developments. This needs to be considered in more detail when considering the scenarios and port planning options. A potential pilot within the Tanger Med bunkering concept seems to be an assessment of the feasibility of ship-to-ship bunkering, in which weather and wave conditions need to be considered.
