By developing 22 scenarios based on the port assessments from Chapter 5, this chapter aims to answer the critical question: What is the best scenario for bunker, export, and industrial demands for allocation and transport among the four selected ports?

Various combinations of production and distribution strategies are explored in these scenarios.
They help us determine the optimal and most cost-effective approaches for integrating green fuels into the maritime industry. By evaluating different production sites, transportation methods, and bunkering options, we aim to outline the pathways that best align with economic and environmental goals.

The analyses and findings have been split into sub-categories to make perceptible conclusions for the scenarios. This enables the identification of the most attractive option per function (hydrogen production, export, bunker fuel, integration) and per port (Tanger Med, Jorf Lasfar, Mohammedia,
Tan-Tan). This systematic approach provides stakeholders with clear insights into the most viable value chains for green hydrogen-based fuels.

Certain assumptions are made as part of the modelling exercise. The results of each scenario are discussed in Section 6.3 onwards. It first shows where hydrogen can be produced at the lowest cost.
It then evaluates which port would be best suited for exporting hydrogen derivatives. Section 6.5 delves into the cost of bunkering ammonia vs methanol at the best location for bunkering. Because no port offers the best location for all three of the desired functions, a series of integrated scenarios are analyzed in Section 6.6. Appendix A9 assesses each scenario in terms of spatial feasibility.
Finally, a preferred set of functions for each port is identified, with Jorf Lasfar split between a focus on hydrogen and hydrogen derivatives.

A combined conclusion on the most attractive scenarios and options has been derived from these sub-conclusions called the Lighthouse Scenario, presented in Section 6.7.

6.1 Developing scenarios to optimize the hydrogen value chain
