 7.3.4 Contracts for difference
 Contracts for difference are usually applied to producers. Still, they can be deployed to ensure that
 renewable energy buyers are compensated for incremental costs compared to the fossil energy
 sources they would otherwise use.

 The United States has set up a mechanism under the Inflation Reduction Act, providing up to
