7.5 Conclusion and summary of financial analysis findings
The comprehensive analysis of green hydrogen-based fuels in Morocco highlights both the potential and challenges associated with their development. The financial analysis builds on the costs as determined in the LCOH/LCOA analysis and assesses whether the product (ammonia) can be competitive and affordable. Morocco’s green hydrogen-based fuels have demonstrated competitive pricing relative to international alternatives. However, the significant affordability gap between green hydrogen-based fuels and unabated fossil fuels remains a substantial hurdle. Addressing this gap is critical to achieve financial viability and requires a strategic approach incorporating various financial and regulatory measures.

The financial analysis concluded that combining interventions will be required to make green hydrogen-based fuels viable and affordable for end users. The current financial viability of green hydrogen-based fuels is constrained by a considerable gap compared to fossil fuels. To close this gap, it is recommended to explore a range of supportive measures:

•   Concessional finance: Offering favorable financial terms to reduce the burden of initial
    investments.

•   Carbon pricing: Implementing mechanisms to price carbon emissions effectively.

•   Carbon contracts for difference: Providing contracts that ensure stable revenue for
    low-carbon projects.

•   Green transportation premiums: Introducing incentives to encourage the use of green
    transportation fuels.

Regulatory compliance is anticipated to drive the adoption of green hydrogen-based fuels, particularly through stringent regulations from the EU, IMO, and other jurisdictions. Monitoring and aligning with international regulatory dynamics will be crucial to ensure that Moroccan green hydrogen-based fuels meet market demand and capitalize on emerging opportunities. The regulatory framework will play a pivotal role in establishing the hydrogen and derivatives market.

Achieving the financial and economic feasibility of green hydrogen-based fuels in Morocco requires a strategic combination of financial mechanisms and regulatory support. Ongoing efforts to explore and implement these measures will be crucial for maximizing the potential of green hydrogen-based fuels and contributing to Morocco’s energy transition and sustainable development goals.

