Mohammedia, Tanger Med, and Jorf Lasfar. However, carbon sources will be needed for methanol production, so these should be explored as soon as possible. To this end, GIZ (Tanmia, 2024)
has launched a study evaluating available carbon sources and carbon demand for hydrogen-based fuel production in five areas. The study results will likely be available by the end of 2025.

Furthermore, an integrated value chain at scale is envisaged in the long term. This will require significant hydrogen (derivatives) production facilities and the development of a key pipeline system for hydrogen—the so-called national hydrogen backbone—which could also be connected internationally.

