9.5 Next steps
The study has identified three high-level pathways, outlining potential opportunities for the four ports considered over different time horizons: short-term focus (<2030), medium-term focus
(2030-2040), and long-term focus (>2040).

In the short term (to 2030), key events include the development of pilot projects for the production and supply of green hydrogen-based bunker fuels in Moroccan ports, in particular, a pilot for methanol bunkering at Tanger Med port, monitoring the progress of renewable energy projects, and assessing the potential demand for green methanol and green ammonia in the selected ports.

In the medium term (to 2040), key events include establishing infrastructure for the production and supply of green hydrogen-based bunker fuels, implementing policies and regulations related to the production and use of e-methanol and e-ammonia, and developing partnerships with other ports to enhance the supply of green hydrogen-based bunker fuels in the region.

In the long term (to 2050), key events include scaling up the production of green methanol and green ammonia, investing in viable carbon sources, and monitoring and adapting to global market dynamics and regulations related to the shipping industry and the use of green hydrogen-based fuels.
